  explanation: 'Data travels across a network as packets, passing through routers on the way to a server. The client sends an HTTP request (a method and an endpoint), the server processes it, may read or change data in the database, and sends back an HTTP response with a status code and usually a JSON body. The moving sphere is a conceptual picture: an HTTP message and a real network packet are not the same thing.'
